{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrtYmY1gKT44VAq8bjst","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BVHnrdMLgryCBbDp3tTYF","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'plan-pedigree-brief',\n  description: 'Parallel readers for the one-a-day plan phase: knowledge contract, neighbour templates, pedigree geometry feasibility',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Read', detail: 'knowledge docs, neighbours, feasibility' }],\n}\nphase('Read')\nconst ROOT = 'C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day'\nconst common = `Repo: ${ROOT} (an m0saic template repo, one template a day). READ ONLY: do not edit, create or delete any file; do not run git commands that change state; do not run npm run build/new. Be fast: you have about 5 minutes. Return a compact plain-text report (<= 700 words), facts only, with file paths.`\nconst tasks = [\n  { label: 'knowledge', prompt: `${common}\nTask: extract the rules a PLANNER must respect for a new template that draws a 5-generation pedigree chart (31 rectangles: Ahnentafel 1..31, generation g has 2^(g-1) cells, laid out as columns: [cell n | (P(2n) over P(2n+1))]) with text in every cell (name, birth year, place) plus a colour legend strip with swatches and counts.\nRead: node_modules/@m0saic/knowledge/docs/templates/philosophy-and-contract.md, docs/templates/construction-strategy.md, docs/handbook/feasibility-precision-quantization.md (skim), and src/_shared/layout.ts (the layout contract helpers: tag, textFits, textFitsMeasured, textFitsAll, TEXT_EM, within/yFrac, minWidthFrac, aspect, sweepLayout). Also src/_shared/ for any text-fit / svgLabel / font-measure helpers (list names + one line each).\nReport: (1) the exact constraint kinds the layout contract supports and their option names; (2) TEXT_EM values; (3) minimum legible text px or any floor the gate enforces; (4) split rules relevant here (1:1 binary splits, depth limits, 5-smooth >12); (5) anything about lists/arrays of props (is a JSON/list prop type supported? how are props typed: string, number, color, boolean, enum, json?); (6) any rule about how many props, defaults, ASCII.` },\n  { label: 'neighbours', prompt: `${common}\nTask: survey neighbour templates so a planner can mirror existing shapes. Look in src/*/ (packs: basics, community, dev, events, gaming, music, science, social, sports) and src/*/registry.ts.\nSpecifically read: src/sports/chess-game-recap/v3 (64 square cells + per-piece rects, a platform knob), src/science/astro-integration-summary/v1, and one or two templates that take a LIST of rows as a prop (grep for props typed as json / array / textarea / 'list' / CSV-like strings — e.g. how a template accepts many rows of data: a multi-line string parsed per line? a JSON prop?). Also check if any template has a legend of colour swatches with counts.\nReport: (1) how list-shaped data is passed as props in this repo (exact prop type/kind used, parsing convention, an example default); (2) how colours are props (type name); (3) the platform/aspect knob pattern in chess v3 if any (prop name, values); (4) what packs exist and whether 'personal' or 'community' fits genealogy best (read community/registry.ts descriptions); (5) typical prop count; (6) still-vs-video: which are stills and how outputHints/format is set; (7) how neighbours handle dense grids at the 480x270 contract canvas (any 'compact' / drop-row logic, text floors).` },\n  { label: 'feasibility', prompt: `${common}\nTask: geometry feasibility for a 5-generation pedigree chart template rendered at the seven contract canvases 1920x1080, 1280x720, 1080x1920, 1080x1080, 3840x2160, 640x360, 480x270. The chart: 31 ancestor cells, Ahnentafel numbering, generations as columns (gen1 = 1 cell full height, gen5 = 16 stacked cells), plus a title strip and a legend strip (up to ~8 swatches with label + count).\nFirst read src/_shared/layout.ts and any font/text measuring helpers in src/_shared (TEXT_EM.prose etc.) to learn the char-width em used for fits, and any minimum-font floor checked by the gate (grep tools/check-layout.mjs and tools/check-registry.mjs for 'minPx', 'floor', 'legib', 'fontPx' — reading tools/ is allowed, editing is not).\nThen compute, for each canvas, with title strip ~10% height and legend ~12% (landscape: legend as bottom band; portrait: consider generations as ROWS top-to-bottom instead, i.e. a rotated pedigree where gen5 is 16 side-by-side cells), the gen-5 cell height/width in px, the font px that fits one line of a ~18-char name ('Margaret Lindqvist') and a 4-char year, using cell*0.94-2px. Recommend: (a) whether one layout (columns) works at all aspects or whether portrait should rotate the tree; (b) what copy per cell is realistic at gen 5 (name only? surname only? initials?) vs gen 1-3 (name + years + place); (c) whether 480x270 can show gen-5 text at all, and what the template should do there (drop text tier, show only colour + number). Give numbers in a small table.` },\n]\nconst results = await parallel(tasks.map(t => () => agent(t.prompt, { label: t.label, phase: 'Read' })))\nreturn tasks.map((t, i) => `=== ${t.label} ===\\n${results[i] || '(no result)'}`).join('\\n\\n')\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":49024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":697},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46f0c3f2-336c-4ef6-8157-cd9cb5b4cbf6","uuid":"da9a2bfd-3945-479e-ad5a-d21a84c61a65","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:20:57.229Z","request_id":"req_011CfrtYmEuyjjVfAGVgeSki","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013BVHnrdMLgryCBbDp3tTYF":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'plan-pedigree-brief',\n  description: 'Parallel