{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7uWWoEj268YTpPgAKwdFp","type":"tool_result","content":"Fri Oct  9 08:23:54 PDT 2026\n=== neighbours ===\nPaths below are relative to C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day.\n\n**(1) Passing list-shaped data as props.** The repo uses two prop kinds for this.\n- **`type: \"list\"` with `fields: {...}`.** Each row is typed in the props UI.\n  - `src/sports/swim-time-drop-card/v1/swim-time-drop-card.ts:104` has `swims` with fields event/entry/final/standard (all strings) and `meta.constraints {minItems:1, maxItems:MAX_SWIMS}`. The description says 1 to 8 rows.\n  - `src/dev/bench-delta/v1/bench-delta.ts:188` has `rows` with name, unit, base, baseRange, value, range; `maxItems: 32`, and only 8 are drawn.\n  - `src/harness/agent-timeline/v1/agent-timeline.ts:116` also uses it.\n- **`type: \"json\"` with `meta.constraints.jsonSchema`.**\n  - `src/science/astro-integration-summary/v1/astro-integration-summary.ts:798`: `sessions` is an array of `{night, filter, frames, exposureSec}`, maxItems MAX_ROWS=2000. The TS type is `AstroSessionInput[] | string`, so a JSON string is also parsed (line 273). The default is `ASTRO_DEFAULT_SESSIONS`, nine rows such as `{ night: \"2026-09-12\", filter: \"Ha\", frames: 40, exposureSec: 180 }`.\n  - `src/music/radio-top-30-chart/v1/radio-top-30-chart.ts:119`: `rows` is a JSON array of strings, one line per row in the form `\"Artist | Title | Label | LW\"`, 1 to 30 items.\n  - `src/events/bird-walk-sightings/v1/bird-walk-sightings.ts:48`: `rows` is a JSON array of `{commonName, count}` (count is an integer or \"X\"), 1 to 200 items. It pages 8 per card through a `page` prop.\n  - Also `src/sports/cubing-average-card` (json array of strings) and `src/community/weekly-run-report:136` (json object).\n- **CSV or raw paste as a string.** Astro has `csv: type \"string\"` with `meta.control {multiline:true, mono:true, placeholder}`. It reads columns by header name, and a non-empty value replaces `sessions`. Chess has `pgn` the same way, with multiline and mono.\n- **Validation.** `render()` is the gate (\"The schema is documentation; render() is the gate\"). Errors are thrown with the prop path, e.g. `rows[3].count`.\n\n**(2) Colours as props.** These are `type: \"string\"` with `meta: { constraints: { isColor: true }, control: { colorPicker: true, defaultColor: X } }`. Examples: qsl-card:157, weekly-run-report:167, crossword-grid-card:139 (`themeColor`), bench-delta:245, app-store-screenshot-frame:110/116. Internally colours are cast `as MosaicColor`. Astro's per-key palette override is `filterColors: type \"json\"`, an object of `#rrggbb` checked against `HEX=/^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/`.\n\n**(3) Platform knob in chess v3** (`src/sports/chess-game-recap/v3/chess-game-recap.ts`).\n- `CHESS_V3_PLATFORMS = {desktop:1920x1080, square:1080x1080, mobile:1080x1920}`.\n- The prop is `platform: type \"string\"`, `meta.constraints.oneOf: PLATFORM_KEYS`, default \"desktop\".\n- `outputHints` spreads `CHESS_V3_PLATFORMS[DEFAULTS.platform]`.\n- `resolveOutputHints(props)` returns the platform's width and height plus the computed `durationMs`. It never throws; bad input falls back to the defaults. An explicit width and height still win.\n- The 64 square cells come from `BASIS = 360`, so the board side sits on the split lattice.\n- Only chess v3 has `platform`. Others say in the outputHints `note` that they reflow by aspect (e.g. astro: `stacked = W < H*1.3`).\n\n**(4) Packs.**\n- In src: basics, community, dev, events, gaming, harness, music, science, social, sports.\n- `pipeline/config.json` vocabulary: social, dev, music, education, business, science, news, personal, ops, community, sports, events, health, finance. \"personal\" is allowed but has no folder yet, so it would be a new pack and needs one sentence of justification (at most one new pack per day).\n- `src/community/registry.ts` holds qsl-card (ham radio QSL from an ADIF record) and weekly-run-report (a volunteer 5k's weekly results). Both are hobby or club output from a standard record format. Genealogy, which comes from GEDCOM and is a family or society hobby, fits \"community\" as an existing pack. \"personal\" means creating a pack.\n\n**(5) Prop count.** Typically 8 to 13 top-level props, always ending with `debugLayout` (boolean, ui order 99).\n- astro 8, chess v3 10, radio 9, bird-walk 8, crossword 10, qsl 13, weekly-run 8.\n- The raw counts for swim (14) and bench (15) include list sub-fields.\n- Every prop has `ui: {label, order}`, and the main one adds `primary: true`.\n\n**(6) Stills vs video.**\n- Stills use `format: { kind: \"image\", container: \"png\" }`, `durationMs: 2000`, `fps: 30`: qsl-card, weekly-run-report, app-store-screenshot-frame, bench-delta, og-card, bird-walk-sightings, homebrew-serving-card, crossword-grid-card, agent-timeline, radio-top-30-chart.\n- Videos use `format: { kind: \"video\", container: \"mp4\" }` with a `resolveOutputHints` for duration: talk-timer, speedrun-pb-recap, astro (`clipSec`), chess v3. Their tags include \"video\".\n\n**(7) Dense grids at 480x270.** Contract canvases (AGENTS.md:138): 1920x1080, 1280x720, 1080x1920, 1080x1080, 3840x2160, 640x360, 480x270.\n- **Readability floor, then refuse.**\n  - qsl-card:341 `floor = max(1, round(S*10/270))`.\n  - weekly-run-report:407 `floor = max(6, round(S*0.022))`.\n  - Both use `unfit(field)`, which throws \"cannot be fitted on WxH above the Npx readability floor: shorten it or render a larger canvas.\"\n- **Fit ladder.** Text shrinks by about 0.92 per step down to `MIN_PX`: astro `MIN_PX = 7` with `fitOne`/`wrapFit` (long names go to 70% and then two lines). Bench-delta's legend shrinks to `minPx`.\n- **Crossword.** `floorPx = max(8, round(S*0.013))`, then on down to 6. `NUMBER_FLOOR_PX = 6`; clue numbers are dropped below it (`numberPx: 0`).\n- **Radio.** `columns = ceil(n / (wide ? 10 : 15))`. Shared floor 0.85 and alone floor 0.5, refusing below that. Its WHY text says there is no pixel floor, so 480x270 is a thumbnail.\n- **Paging instead of shrinking.** bird-walk-sightings shows 8 per page with a `page` prop; its note reads \"Minimum tested canvas 480x270.\"\n- **Row caps.** Bench-delta draws 8 rows; swim allows 1 to 8 (\"split a longer meet across two cards\").\n\n**Legend of colour swatches with counts.** None exactly.\n- Bench-delta (lines 423-875) has the fullest legend: one entry per channel, several swatches per verdict, type that shrinks until it fits. Its text is run labels, not counts.\n- Crossword has `theme-swatch` square rects beside list lines (lines 439, 550, 739), bound to `themeColor`, with aspect and equal-size constraints.\n- Astro colours its legend swatches per filter (`filterColors`), and its bars show hours.\n- Bird-walk's \"legend\" is only the text line \"X = observed, not counted\".\n\nShared helpers: `src/_shared/text.ts` (budget, widthOf, wrapFit, textCell), `src/_shared/layout.ts` (textFitsMeasured, withLayoutIntent), `src/_shared/why.ts`.\n\n=== feasibility ===\nColumns work at every contract canvas, so I wouldn't rotate the tree in portrait. Gen 5 has room for one line of copy in landscape and square. At 480x270 it gets about 8.6px, so the template should show only colour plus the Ahnentafel number there.\n\n**What the code says**\n- `src/_shared/layout.ts`: `TEXT_EM = { prose: 0.52, caps: 0.66, url: 0.6 }` (Roboto measurement plus a 12% margin); the contract's own default is 0.72. `CONTRACT_CANVASES` holds the 7-canvas set.\n- `src/_shared/text.ts`: `budget(cellW) = max(8, floor(cellW*0.94 - 2))`. `fitLine` shrinks a line by ×0.92 steps down to a `minPx` the template picks.\n- `@m0saic/template-utils` `textFits` estimates longest line × fontSize × charWidthEm and checks it against the box. It is width only. `textEmUnits(\"Margaret Lindqvist\") = 18`, `\"1874\" = 4`.\n- **The gate has no minimum font size.** `tools/check-layout.mjs` checks that every text has a `textFits` and that the intent holds at all 7 canvases, nothing about legibility. `tools/check-registry.mjs` has nothing on fonts either. Floors are set per template:\n  - 10px: `src/dev/og-card/v1/og-card.ts`\n  - 8px: `src/social/testimonial-proof-card/v1/testimonial-proof-card.ts`\n  - 7px: `src/science/astro-integration-summary/v1/astro-integration-summary.ts`\n  - 6px for numbers: `src/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1/crossword-grid-card.ts`\n- Real Roboto widths I measured: name 0.462 em/char, digits 0.562 em/char. The 0.52 prose ruler is too narrow for years (\"1874\" is 2.25em). Use `textFitsMeasured` or about 0.6 em for digit strings.\n\n**Assumptions:** title is 10% of H and the legend 12% of H (bottom band), so the chart gets 0.78H. No gutters; real gutters take roughly another 5–10%. Font sizes come from (cell*0.94−2) / (18×0.52) for width and (h*0.94−2) / (1.2×lines) for height. \"Rows\" is the rotated tree (gen 5 as 16 side-by-side cells).\n\n| canvas | COLS gen5 w×h | 1-line name | name/year (2 lines) | gen3 w×h, 3 lines | ROWS gen5 w×h | ROWS name | ROWS year | legend 8×1 / 4×2 (12 chars) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1920x1080 | 384×52.6 | 38.4 | 19.8 | 384×211, 38.4 | 120×169 | 11.8 | 48.3 | 35.8 / 49.1 |\n| 1280x720 | 256×35.1 | 25.5 | 12.9 | 256×140, 25.5 | 80×112 | 7.8 | 31.9 | 23.8 / 32.2 |\n| 1080x1920 | 216×93.6 | 21.5 | 21.5 | 216×374, 21.5 | 67.5×300 | 6.6 | 26.8 | 20.0 / 40.4 |\n| 1080x1080 | 216×52.6 | 21.5 | 19.8 | 216×211, 21.5 | 67.5×169 | 6.6 | 26.8 | 20.0 / 40.4 |\n| 3840x2160 | 768×105 | 76.9 | 40.4 | 768×421, 76.9 | 240×337 | 23.9 | 97.4 | 72.0 / 99.9 |\n| 640x360 | 128×17.6 | 12.1 | 6.0 | 128×70, 12.6 | 40×56 | 3.8 | 15.5 | 11.7 / 15.3 |\n| 480x270 | 96×13.2 | 8.6 | 4.3 | 96×53, 9.4 | 30×42 | 2.8 | 11.4 | 8.7 / 11.0 |\n\n**(a) One layout or rotate in portrait?**\n- Keep columns everywhere. Rotating makes gen 5 only W/16 wide (67px at 1080), so a horizontal name drops to 6.6px.\n- Portrait columns give gen 5 cells of 216×94, which fit name and year on two lines at 21.5px. That is the best gen-5 case below 4K.\n- I did not check whether svg text layers support rotated or vertical text.\n- In landscape and square, gen 5 is limited by height (16 stacked rows), so making the gen-5 column wider does not help.\n- What helps is giving gen 5 more height. Moving the legend to a right-hand side column in landscape raises gen-5 height to 0.9H/16. At 480x270 that is 15.2px tall, about 10.2px for one line, but the narrower columns then fit only a surname.\n\n**(b) Copy per generation tier**\n- **Gen 5, landscape and square:** one line only. The full name fits at 1280x720 and above (25–77px). Two lines (name/year) only work at 1920x1080 and 4K, around 20px or more. At 1280x720 two lines give 12.9px, so drop years there.\n- **Gen 5, portrait:** name plus years on two lines at 21.5px.\n- **Gen 4** (8 cells, twice gen 5's height): name plus years on two lines everywhere down to 640x360 (about 12px).\n- **Gen 1–3:** name, years and place on three lines. With five equal columns these tiers are limited by width, because the 18-char name sets the size (9.4px at 480x270, 38px at 1080p). Wrapping the name onto two lines (\"Margaret\" / \"Lindqvist\", 9 units) roughly doubles it, and the cells have the height for that (gen 3 at 480x270 is 53px tall).\n- **Suggested rule:** for each cell, pick the richest tier whose `min(widthFit, heightFit)` is at or above a chosen floor (10px suggested). Order: name+years+place, then name/years, then name, then surname, then Ahnentafel number, then colour only. Give each tier its own label so `mergeTextFits` doesn't take the widest em.\n\n**(c) 480x270 (and 640x360)**\n- **480x270:** gen 5 is 96×13.2, so one line at most 8.6px and two lines 4.3px. The gate would pass 8.6px (no floor), but it is below the 10px og-card floor. Recommendation: gen 5 shows colour plus the Ahnentafel number (\"16\"–\"31\", fits at 8.6px, height-bound). Gen 4 shows a surname. Gen 1–3 show the wrapped name only, with years dropped below about 10px.\n- **640x360:** gen 5 can show a full name or surname at about 12px on one line, no years.\n- **Legend:** use a 4×2 grid rather than 8×1 at the two small canvases (11.0 vs 8.7px at 480x270, 15.3 vs 11.7px at 640x360).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46f0c3f2-336c-4ef6-8157-cd9cb5b4cbf6","uuid":"85ad257d-0d8b-4ae2-9dc3-098a80e48670","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:23:55.018Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Fri Oct  9 08:23:54 PDT 2026\n=== neighbours ===\nPaths below are relative to C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day.\n\n**(1) Passing list-shaped data as props.** The repo uses two prop kinds for this.\n- **`type: \"list\"` with `fields: {...}`.** Each row is typed in the props UI.\n  - `src/sports/swim-time-drop-card/v1/swim-time-drop-card.ts:104` has `swims` with fields event/entry/final/standard (all strings) and `meta.constraints {minItems:1, maxItems:MAX_SWIMS}`. The description says 1 to 8 rows.\n  - `src/dev/bench-delta/v1/bench-delta.ts:188` has `rows` with name, unit, base, baseRange, value, range; `maxItems: 32`, and only 8 are drawn.\n  - `src/harness/agent-timeline/v1/agent-timeline.ts:116` also uses it.\n- **`type: \"json\"` with `meta.constraints.jsonSchema`.**\n  - `src/science/astro-integration-summary/v1/astro-integration-summary.ts:798`: `sessions` is an array of `{night, filter, frames, exposureSec}`, maxItems MAX_ROWS=2000. The TS type is `AstroSessionInput[] | string`, so a JSON string is also parsed (line 273). The default is `ASTRO_DEFAULT_SESSIONS`, nine rows such as `{ night: \"2026-09-12\", filter: \"Ha\", frames: 40, exposureSec: 180 }`.\n  - `src/music/radio-top-30-chart/v1/radio-top-30-chart.ts:119`: `rows` is a JSON array of strings, one line per row in the form `\"Artist | Title | Label | LW\"`, 1 to 30 items.\n  - `src/events/bird-walk-sightings/v1/bird-walk-sightings.ts:48`: `rows` is a JSON array of `{commonName, count}` (count is an integer or \"X\"), 1 to 200 items. It pages 8 per car