{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfru2Ev46UdWSfSCZvkV5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WjbDQ3Sr242zkptBHZSDg7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');const p='journal/2026-10-09/20-brief.md';let t=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!t.includes(a))throw new Error('missing: '+a.slice(0,60));t=t.replace(a,b)};\nrep(/Expected at defaults: 1920x1080 is T0[^\\n]*/.exec(t)[0],\n'The ladder is computed, not hard-coded per canvas. 1280x720 and 3840x2160 are 1920x1080 scaled, so they choose the same tiers. The test records the chosen tier per generation per canvas as a snapshot. The one hard minimum: at 1920x1080 every generation shows at least name and year (T1), because gen-5 cells there are about 380x50 px and fit two lines at about 18 px. At 480x270 gen 5 is about 96x12 px, which leaves one line at the 7 px floor, so expect T2-T4 there.');\nrep('2. **Chrome lives where the design says.** \\`title\\` within \\`yFrac [0, 0.18]\\`. \\`legend\\` within \\`yFrac [0.6, 1]\\` and full width (\\`minWidthFrac 0.9\\`). The \\`chart\\` region overlaps neither band.',\n'2. **Chrome lives where the design says.** \\`title\\` within \\`yFrac [0, 0.18]\\`. \\`legend\\` within \\`yFrac [0.6, 1]\\` and full width (\\`minWidthFrac 0.9\\`). \\`chart\\` within \\`yFrac [0.05, 0.95]\\`. The contract has no non-overlap constraint, so the test asserts from the rects that the chart does not overlap the title or the legend.');\nrep('3. **Presence.** \\`title\\`, \\`chart\\` and \\`legend\\` always render. Exactly 31 \\`ancestor-cell\\` rects, known or unknown, always (a one-to-many label with count 31). Every legend entry has a swatch.',\n'3. **Presence.** \\`title\\`, \\`chart\\`, \\`legend\\` and the five cell labels \\`ancestor-cell-g1\\` ... \\`ancestor-cell-g5\\` (bare \\`{ label }\\`) always render. The contract has no count field, so the test asserts the counts from the resolved rects: 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16 cells, 31 in total, known or unknown, and one swatch per legend entry.');\nrep('4. **The tree is exact.** Within each generation the cells are equal height (allow +-1 px of quantization), and cell n spans 2n and 2n+1 (top of n = top of 2n, bottom of n = bottom of 2n+1, within 1 px). Columns are equal width (+-1 px). The test asserts this from the emitted rects. If \\`relations\\` can express it, the contract states it too.',\n'4. **The tree is exact.** In the contract, \\`relations\\` holds one \\`{ label: \\\"ancestor-cell-gK\\\", equal: \\\"height\\\", tolerancePx: 1 }\\` per generation and \\`{ label: [all five], equal: \\\"width\\\", tolerancePx: 1 }\\`. Use \\`tolerancePx\\`, because the default relative 2% fails at 480x270, where gen-5 cells are 11-12 px. Only the test can check the spans, since no constraint compares edges across labels: top of n = top of 2n and bottom of n = bottom of 2n+1, within 1 px, from the emitted rects.');\nrep('\\`n\\` is the Ahnentafel number 1-31. \\`year\\` may be empty.','\\`n\\` is the Ahnentafel number 1-31. \\`year\\` may be empty, or match \\`^(c\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\s?)?\\\\\\\\d{3,4}\\$\\` (\\\"1850\\\", \\\"c. 1850\\\"), the same form the GEDCOM path produces.');\nrep('A duplicate n, n outside 1-31, or a year that is not 3-4 digits is refused','A duplicate n, an n outside 1-31, or a year outside that form is refused');\nrep('It walks FAMC to HUSB/WIFE from the root to fill Ahnentafel 1-31.','It walks FAMC to HUSB/WIFE from the root to fill Ahnentafel 1-31. When a person has several FAMC (birth and adoptive), it follows the one with \\`PEDI birth\\` and otherwise the first.');\nrep('\\`homeCountry\\` · string · \\\"USA\\\" · the country whose places key by state. Matching is case-insensitive, and \\\"United States\\\", \\\"United States of America\\\", \\\"US\\\" and \\\"U.S.A.\\\" all fold to \\\"USA\\\".',\n'\\`homeCountry\\` · string · \\\"USA\\\" · the country whose places key by state. Matching is case-insensitive. \\\"United States\\\", \\\"United States of America\\\", \\\"US\\\" and \\\"U.S.A.\\\" all fold to \\\"USA\\\", and the fold also applies to every place\\\\'s last element before keying, in both \\`keyBy\\` modes. So \\\"..., United States\\\" and \\\"..., USA\\\" never become two legend keys.');\nrep('The legend keeps its colours but drops the counts. Same props','The legend is unchanged, counts included. Same props');\nrep('saturated Office-style fills (the look people screenshot in the Facebook groups), with bold black cell text.','saturated Office-style fills (the look people screenshot in the Facebook groups), with bold cell text. The text colour is still chosen by luminance, not forced black: black on Office blue is about 4.45:1, under the 4.5:1 rubric floor.');\nfs.writeFileSync(p,t);console.log('ok');\n\" && grep -n -E \"c\\\\\\\\.|PEDI|tolerancePx|snapshot\" journal/2026-10-09/20-brief.md | cut -c1-160; date","description":"Apply skeptic fixes to the brief"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4508,"cache_read_input_tokens":110405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4508},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46f0c3f2-336c-4ef6-8157-cd9cb5b4cbf6","uuid":"d6c3b775-e570-462b-81db-8d308e06b493","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:27:06.330Z","request_id":"req_011Cfru2EcT6keunqa6FPCry","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WjbDQ3Sr242zkptBHZSDg7":{"command":"cd /c/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');const p='journal/2026-10-09/20-brief.md';let t=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!t.includes(a))throw new Error('missing: '+a.slice(0,60));t=t.replace(a,b)};\nrep(/Expected at defaults: 1920x1080